{"schema_version":1,"run_id":"p4-setc-full-r1","system":"full","paper_id":"2002.02798v3","variant":"original","error_class":"method_mismatch","anchor":{"kind":"document"},"target":{"kind":"setting","key":"method"},"state":"needs_human_review","summary":"The CIFAR-10 training script does not set '--solver rk4' or '--step_size 0.25' (unlike mnist.sh), leaving the solver to default to the adaptive Dormand-Prince ('dopri5') solver instead of the 4-stage Runge-Kutta solver with step size 0.25.","evidence":[{"kind":"quote","source":{"kind":"submission","id":"2002.02798v3","title":null,"url":null},"text":"In contrast, a simple fixed-grid four stage Runge-Kutta solver suffices for RN-ODE during training on MNIST and CIFAR10, using a step size of 0.25.","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":null,"line_start":null,"line_end":null},{"kind":"code","source":{"kind":"repository","id":"https://github.com/cfinlay/ffjord-rnode@8302dfb806284f6c42da0687d6100f4bac45726f","title":null,"url":"https://github.com/cfinlay/ffjord-rnode"},"text":"  ../train.py --data $DATA \\\n  --distributed \\\n  --datadir $DATADIR \\\n  --save $SAVE \\\n  --kinetic-energy $KE \\\n  --jacobian-norm2 $JF \\\n  --alpha 0.05 \\\n  --test_solver dopri5 --test_atol 1e-5 --test_rtol 1e-5 \\","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":"example-scripts/cifar10.sh","line_start":13,"line_end":20}],"finding_id":"code-1cbe3b421c87297d-f0","severity":"high","duplicate_of":null}
